00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.810
What do you think, Ibarada-kun?

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:27.290
It's staggeringly dubious.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.890
And it doesn't really have anything 
to do with the university, does it?

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.320
It's not bad if you think of it as a joke,

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:38.350
but it's crap as content 
for a promotional brochure.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.060
Professor?

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.810
Why do you care so much about 
strength training anyway?

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:49.830
People these days tend to lack in exercise.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:55.830
Reasonable amounts of training have positive 
effects on the body. That's been proven.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:00.230
And personally, training my 
body has given me confidence.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.230
When I'm having a hard time, if I 
work up a sweat, my mood clears

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.960
and it makes me feel like I can keep trying.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:12.210
I wanted to convey the wonder 
of that to the students, but...

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:18.090
When people don't understand the thing 
you love, it's a lonely feeling, isn't it?

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:25.060
In that case, please think of 
a different way to convey it.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.900
And please don't forget your deadline.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:31.070
Yes, you're right.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.990
What shall I do...?

