00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.000
Professor Ikeda,

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.000
This is Himuro from master's course, year 1.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.000
I have caught a cold and am feeling unwell,

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.000
so I won't be coming to the meeting today.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.000
I am terribly sorry. Thank you.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.870
What's this? What's this?

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:43.000
Science Fell in Love,
So I Tried to Prove It [<b>r=1-sinθ</b>]

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.750
It's rare for Himuro-senpai 
to be absent, isn't it?

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.750
She looked like she was having 
a hard time yesterday.

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.680
Maybe I'll go visit her later.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.840
Don't.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.070
It's just a cold, isn't it?

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.260
It isn't influenza season, after all.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:04.280
Yukimura-senpai, you aren't worried?

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:07.390
She'll be better after two 
or three days of rest.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:08.770
Paying a get-well visit would 
only be a waste of time.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.200
You might be right.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.370
Himuro-senpai is mature and sensible.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.790
If I go, she might feel she 
has to be considerate of me.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.920
I can't get in touch with Himuro, though.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:23.040
<i>He's super worried about her!</i>

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:27.700
That idiot. I'm sure he'll go without 
taking any food or anything with him.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.770
I'll buy something and go after him.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.090
<i>I shouldn't have pushed myself so hard.</i>

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:43.730
<i>Having a cold when you live 
alone is really tough.</i>

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:50.310
<i>When I lived with my mother, 
she often used to take care of me.</i>

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:59.950
Mother, please go to work. I'm fine.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.460
You'll catch my cold, too, Mother.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.040
Sounds good!

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.170
They say that you get better when 
someone else catches it, right?

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:14.010
There is no medical proof of that. 
I read it in a book.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:18.340
Mother, things are difficult at work, right?

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:21.480
I'll be fine on my own.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.940
Why are you talking like 
such a reasonable child?

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.300
You should be more selfish 
when you're sick at least.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:33.250
Then will you talk with me a lot today?

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:36.040
All right.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.990
The idea that a cold gets better when someone 
else catches it is, of course, superstition.

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:43.540
But why would a rumor 
like that be so common?

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:45.130
Why?

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:49.350
"Recovering from a cold" and 
"someone else developing symptoms"

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.640
often occur at the same time.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:56.090
This leads people to mistakenly assume 
a causal relationship between them.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:09:00.250
The idea that people who play violent 
games will commit crimes is the same.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.660
A dream?

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:06.960
"I'll be fine on my own"?

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.630
That wasn't true at all.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.110
I was just pretending to be strong.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.010
Food and water.

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:16.650
I have to go buy some.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.150
I am a science-type.

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.790
No matter the circumstances, 
I can deal with things intellectually.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:25.940
I'm fine on my own now.

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.450
I'm fine...

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:32.790
It's so hard, Mother...

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.270
Mother...

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:38.790
Himuro! Are you all right?!

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:47.690
Hey! Himuro!

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.340
Why did you show up now? Go away!

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.670
What did you say?

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.300
I have preparations that need to be made!

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:56.610
What could you need to prepare?

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.070
Stop saying incomprehensible 
things, and open up!

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:00.720
Honestly!

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:03.870
Yukimura-kun, I don't want you to see 
what I look like when I've just woken up!

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:09.240
All right. If you're fine, then I'll go.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:15.590
Why are you leaving? 
Stay a little longer!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.960
Which is it, you little...!

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:25.340
This is the worst! 
I haven't even cleaned up.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.760
Don't look at my room, you pervert!

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:33.810
Don't look at me, either!

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:35.360
Then where can I look?

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:38.390
I'm sorry for suddenly coming to your place.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:43.490
I thought that someone living alone would 
have trouble preparing food and water.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:46.480
But you came empty-handed, 
didn't you, Yukimura-kun?

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:48.560
Oh.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.850
Really, what did you come here for?

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.000
I couldn't help it, I was in a hurry!

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.820
If something terrible had happened to you...

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:57.250
then...

00:10:58.280 --> 00:10:59.890
I've had enough.

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:26.020
I'm going to give you my cold, Yukimura-kun.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.700
That way, I'll get better.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.230
Huh? That's weird.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:38.160
Yukimura-senpai should be here.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:39.560
Oh. It's open.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:44.010
Himuro-senpai! I came to see you!

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.000
Oh, Kanade-chan!

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.620
I-I'm sorry for just coming in.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:53.360
I brought you a few different... Huh?

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.090
Where's Yukimura-senpai?

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:58.310
Y-Yukimura-kun isn't here.

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:01.480
Huh? But his shoes were there.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:04.360
Sh-Shopping. He went shopping.

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:06.690
Maybe he accidentally went 
wearing house slippers?

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:08.950
Oh...

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:12.110
Wow, thank you for all of these.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:13.870
You're very welcome.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.710
<i>Wh-What is this situation?!</i>

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.120
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:22.220
<i>I don't know why, but I pushed 
Yukimura-kun under the comforter.</i>

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.010
<i>What are you doing, Himuro?!</i>

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.970
<i>If worst comes to worst and 
Kanade sees us like this...</i>

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.050
Himuro-senpai, how are you feeling?

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:35.230
I'm all right. Thank you for taking 
the trouble to come visit me.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:38.520
<i>But... what could this sweet scent be?</i>

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:42.430
<i>Blast it! Think of something else!</i>

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:44.730
<i>Think about outer space!</i>

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:49.360
<i>I am the universe.</i>

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:54.600
<i>In outer space, they say that ethyl 
formate creates a sweet scent...</i>

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:57.960
<i>That's right. This is, indeed...</i>

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.870
<i>the eternal cosmos.</i>

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.480
<i>I am a planet.</i>

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:05.560
<i>Following Kepler's first 
law of planetary motion...</i>

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.020
<i>I am a planet traveling 
a large, circular orbit.</i>

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.820
<i>This is space.</i>

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:13.060
<i>I am a planet.</i>

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.330
<i>This is space.</i>

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:19.520
Blast it.

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:25.480
...three...

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:27.490
...four...

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:34.180
Why is she suddenly doing strength training?

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.490
<i>Is it part of a diet?</i>

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:39.950
This is the worst. 
I'm covered in sweat.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.230
I should never have done it.

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:45.390
What about this is "wonderful"?

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.080
Let's see. Next is...

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:53.000
Good morning.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.530
Oh, is your cold better now?

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:57.750
Yes, completely better.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:59.510
It's pretty impressive.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:02.510
Oh, dear. What's this?

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:06.690
This time, it seems that 
Yukimura-kun is feeling poorly.

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:07.780
I'm fine.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:12.320
I was thinking a little about the 
cosmos and tired myself out is all.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:14.690
